Privacy Policy
Effective Date: 10 May 2026
Cricket Turf is a single-player offline cricket simulation game developed by Sandip Rathod.
This Privacy Policy explains how we collect, use, and protect your information when you use our mobile application.
1. Information We Collect
We collect the following information:

Photos (Optional): When you add a photo to a player profile, the photo is stored locally on your device only. We do not upload, transmit, or store these photos on any server.
Advertising Data: We use Google AdMob to show interstitial advertisements. AdMob may collect certain device and usage data for the purpose of showing relevant ads. This data is collected and processed by Google in accordance with Google’s Privacy Policy.

We do not collect:

Names, email addresses, or any other personal identifiers
Location data
Any account or login information (the app does not require login)
How We Use Your Information

Photos are used only to display the player’s picture inside the game.
Advertising data is used by Google AdMob to show ads and measure ad performance.

3. Third-Party Services
We use Google AdMob (a third-party advertising service).
Google’s Privacy Policy: https://policies.google.com/privacy
4. Children’s Privacy (COPPA)
Our app is not directed to children under the age of 13. We do not knowingly collect personal information from children under 13.
5. Data Sharing
We do not sell your personal data.
The only third party that may receive data is Google (through AdMob for advertising purposes).
6. Data Storage and Security
All player data and photos are stored locally on your device using Apple’s SwiftData framework. No data is uploaded to our servers.
7. Your Rights
You can delete any player or photo directly inside the app. You can also clear all data using the “Clear All Data” option in the app.
Changes to This Privacy Policy
We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. We will notify you of any changes by updating the Effective Date.
